# Release script configuration (scripts/release.sh)
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you want. The .env file is
# git-ignored. Every variable here is OPTIONAL: with no .env (or an empty
# CHANGELOG_AI_PROVIDER) the release script still works and generates the
# changelog from a grouped list of commit messages.
#
# Both providers are OpenAI-compatible HTTP APIs and require an API key.

# AI provider used to write the CHANGELOG section.
#   opencode -> opencode Go (https://opencode.ai/docs/go)
#   openai   -> OpenAI, or any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint
#   (empty)  -> skip AI, fall back to a grouped commit list
CHANGELOG_AI_PROVIDER=opencode

# Model id (plain, no provider prefix).
#   opencode: required, e.g. deepseek-v4.1-flash, kimi-k2.7-code, glm-5.3
#   openai:   optional, defaults to gpt-4o-mini
CHANGELOG_AI_MODEL=deepseek-v4.1-flash

# --- Required when CHANGELOG_AI_PROVIDER=opencode ---
# Your opencode Go API key (from https://opencode.ai/auth).
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# Base URL (defaults to https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1; rarely needs changing).
# OPENCODE_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1
# If the Go call fails (e.g. the usage limit is reached), the script retries on
# OpenCode Zen's free models (ids ending in "-free"): the free variant of
# CHANGELOG_AI_MODEL first, then the others, up to 5 attempts. The free tier
# only answers the opencode CLI, so that fallback needs `opencode` on PATH,
# using its own login (`opencode auth login`), not the key above.

# --- Required when CHANGELOG_AI_PROVIDER=openai ---
# API key for the OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Base URL of the endpoint (defaults to https://api.openai.com/v1).
# Point this at any OpenAI-compatible provider (OpenRouter, Groq, local, ...).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
